{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested — R1 revision 13 at exact head 7efb0f7f0fe601b7280adf4d68d0bc011233443b. Ordinary whole-scope, evidence-only review under invitation 660a2a00 and original commission c75205df; primary 5c949edb followed by corrections 944d4811, lane companion b6f2dc97 and inventory e4d5fe6d. This is the replacement filing, not the retired 29a invitation.\n\nP2 — Count every fetched fact in the retained-byte reservation. In notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md:3084–3096, DH4/DI4 now fetches and retains every foreign fact of a declared field, including an unused or copy-only field. The normative retained-input count at line 9483 still counts only fact fields/presented facts read by a fact guard or a part needing their bytes (formula and no-sharing rule at 9462–9502). A settling form can declare a bounded list of distinct valid foreign facts, within its field and foreign-entry bounds, and never read them with a guard or part. That count includes none of the list although admission now retains all of it; the delivery source is a separate input. Therefore the stated calculation is not a maximum for newly retained bytes. The guarantee at 9557–9559 that settling work fits its own reservation in every dimension cannot follow from this calculation.\n\nCorrect the existing normative count to cover every fetched declared fact recursively through typed records/lists, plus presented facts and the delivery source once, using the existing declared maxima. Preserve the existing capacity follow-through ownership and use an existing pure reservation witness. This is a structural undercount: I claim no actual overflow at current R4 numeric limits, runtime failure or executed witness. No new mechanism, gate or commission is needed.\n\nCoverage: the same n4 reader had personal full coverage of all four subjects at adopted 53 and e008, verified unchanged-byte transfers, then personally read the complete e008→7ef U3 delta, all additions/removals/context t